 * static-analysis engine.
 *
 * <h3>Design principles</h3>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>Each test is derived from the finding's rule ID, file, line number,
 *       and the evidence snippet embedded in the finding description.</li>
 *   <li>No AI model, no external API, no randomness — output is 100%
 *       deterministic for a given finding.</li>
 *   <li>Tests are honest: they are marked {@code NOT_RUN} and include a
 *       clear comment stating they have not been executed.</li>
 *   <li>When the evidence is available, it is embedded verbatim as a comment
 *       so the developer knows exactly which line triggered the finding.</li>
 *   <li>When context is insufficient for a real assertion, a scaffold is
 *       generated with an explicit {@code // SCAFFOLD} comment explaining
 *       what must be implemented before the test has value.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <h3>Supported rule IDs</h3>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>{@code SQLI-001} — SQL injection via string concatenation</li>
 *   <li>{@code CRED-001} — Hardcoded credential literal</li>
 *   <li>{@code EXEC-001} — Dangerous command execution</li>
 *   <li>{@code DESER-001} — Unsafe deserialization</li>
 *   <li>Any other rule → generic scaffold</li>
 * </ul>
